      "basis": "The fresh 0.4–3.5 s pitch overlay and independent attacks at 0.940, 1.103 and 1.393 s identify the source opening A4–D5–A4 after 0.75 quarter of written rests. Reject the broad first window’s 1.38 s rise (peak 1.40 s): it selects the third note’s repeated A4 and compresses the first two notes to milliseconds despite passing numeric gates. Restrict the first anchor to the actual initial A4. The closing D-major sonority begins around 293.6 s in the 292–296.5 s overlay, including new D2 bass energy. Reject the initial broad last window’s 295.52 s decay fluctuation, which delayed the last attack and failed the 0.5 s anchor gate."
    },
